From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d/steamvr_lh: own base station relationship averaging

Average Valve relationship measurements in the Lighthouse driver before
provider Init starts callbacks. Own the estimator for the Context lifetime,
flush on the existing frame thread, and remove hooks after provider Cleanup.
Persist station-pair estimates in config/lighthouse/monado-relations.json.

Default on for supported x86-64 drivers; LH_AVERAGE_RELATIONSHIPS=0 disables
the feature. Unsupported binaries and architectures keep Valve placement.
No external calibration app, companion library or special launcher is needed.

The estimator and guarded Linux hook are adapted from QuestLHSync under MIT;
retain its license and the HDE64 BSD license in the driver source. Test real
Context lifetimes, hook routing, inverse/antipodal poses, outliers, movement,
persistence, invalid state, and environment/default enable/disable behavior.

